-- title:
--   Image of δ is the Cartier-fixed regular differentials
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and assume $F$ is a curve function field over $K$ in the project's sense: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a divisor, i.e. a finitely supported integer-valued function on the places of $K$–$F$ (valuation subrings of $F$, not equal to $\top$, containing the image of $K$ and principal ideal rings) whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ and whose degree is $0$; each residue field of a place is finite over $K$; and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Let $p$ be a prime, let $K$ have characteristic $p$ and be perfect, and let $x \in F$ be such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield generated by $x$ over $K$. Let $C \colon \Omega_{F/K} \to \Omega_{F/K}$ be additive and satisfy the three Cartier identities $C(f^p \cdot \omega) = f \cdot C\omega$, $C(df) = 0$ and $C(f^{p-1}\,df) = df$ for all $f \in F$ and $\omega$. Let $\delta$ be an additive homomorphism from the $p$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(K,F)$ (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones) to $\Omega_{F/K}$ satisfying the recipe: $\delta y = g^{-1}\,dg$ whenever $y$ is represented by a degree-zero divisor $E$ and $g \neq 0$ satisfies $p \cdot E(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}\,g$ at every place $v$. Then the range of $\delta$ is exactly the set of $\omega \in \Omega_{F/K}$ with $C\omega = \omega$ and $\omega$ regular, i.e. $v.\mathrm{ord}$ of the coefficient of $\omega$ with respect to a uniformizer at $v$ is $\geq 0$ for every place $v$.
--
--   This is the classical description, going back to Serre, of the $p$-torsion of the Jacobian of a curve in characteristic $p$: the logarithmic differentials $g^{-1}dg$ attached to $p$-torsion divisor classes are precisely the regular differentials fixed by the Cartier operator. It is used in the count of $p$-torsion in the Picard group of a modular curve against the space of Cartier-fixed regular differentials on its function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_range_eq_setOf_cartier_fixed_and_isRegularDiff.lean

import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Differentials

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open KaehlerDifferential AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.range_eq_setOf_cartier_fixed_and_isRegularDiff
    {K : Type u} {F : Type v} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F]
    [AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver K F] [HasPrincipalDivisors K F]
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP K p] [PerfectField K]
    (x : F) [FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F]
    (C : Ω[F⁄K] →+ Ω[F⁄K])
    (hsemi : ∀ (f : F) (ω : Ω[F⁄K]), C (f ^ p • ω) = f • C ω)
    (hker : ∀ f : F, C (D K F f) = 0)
    (hlog : ∀ f : F, C (f ^ (p - 1) • D K F f) = D K F f)
    (δ : Pic0.torsion K F p →+ Ω[F⁄K])
    (hδ : ∀ (y : Pic0.torsion K F p) (E : Divisor.degZero (K := K) (F := F)) (g : F),
        Pic0.mk E = (y : Pic0 K F) → g ≠ 0 →
        (∀ v : Place K F, (p : ℤ) * (E : Divisor K F) v = v.ord g) →
        δ y = g⁻¹ • D K F g) :
    Set.range δ = {ω : Ω[F⁄K] | C ω = ω ∧ AlgebraicCurve.IsRegularDiff K F ω} := by sorry
